WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.974
Python follows an order of operations just like
standard arithmetic Multiplication

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.039
and division are evaluated before addition and
subtraction unless parentheses change the grouping
This

00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:18.671
matters because a calculation can be syntactically
valid but still produce the wrong analytical result

00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:25.921
Python may not give you an error message if your
formula is grouped incorrectly Compare

00:00:25.948 --> 00:00:31.198
ten plus five times two with the same values placed
inside parentheses before the multiplication

00:00:32.135 --> 00:00:38.266
Predict both results first then run the example In
analytical code parentheses

00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:42.608
can make both the intended calculation and the code
itself easier to understand
